  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.0-preview3\n- Suites now run inside a per-suite AsyncServiceScope: scoped services are fresh per\n  suite and disposed at the suite boundary; factory delegates receive the scoped\n  provider (behavior change for AddSuite(factory) consumers).\n- Scope disposal failures are reported as a synthetic \"(suite scope dispose)\" failed\n  result; the run continues and RunAsync still returns a report.\n- Trim-safe registration: AddSuite overloads and the discovery path carry\n  DynamicallyAccessedMembers annotations; the library builds with the trim analyzer\n  enabled and trim diagnostics as errors. Registered suites survive IL-trimmed hosts\n  (verified end-to-end on a trimmed Blazor WebAssembly publish).\n- Targets net10.0 only; net8.0/net9.0 assets removed (both out of support).\n- Dependencies: Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions 10.0.15,\n  Microsoft.Testing.Platform 2.5.3.\n\nv1.0.0-preview2\n- Adds TestRunReportFormatter for canonical plain-text report rendering.\n- Consumers can now call TestRunReportFormatter.Format(report) to produce\n  human-readable output for console, CI logs, bug reports, or any text sink.\n\nv1.0.0-preview1\n- First v1 preview release of Circuids.Pulse.\n- Locks the one-package in-app runner model for real host conformance tests.\n- Marks Pulse ready for real project adoption and production conformance pilots while stable v1 feedback is gathered from the .NET community.\n- Reinforces Pulse conformance tests as an extra runtime verification layer, not a replacement for unit, integration, UI, end-to-end, or other existing test types.\n- Adds v1 report schema metadata and total run duration to TestRunReport.\n- Enforces one active Pulse run per host service provider.\n- Skips suite tests after InitializeAsync failure while still running teardown.\n- Documents the canonical TestSupport / Tests / ConformanceHost structure.\n\nv0.1.1-Experimental\n- Minor fixes for build pipeline.\n\nv0.1.0-Experimental\n- Initial release of Circuids.Pulse",
